  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 8 actions (src/actions.ts) and 7 feedbacks (6 boolean, 1 advanced; src/feedbacks.ts). Both are single object literals registered at the end of their function, nothing is generated at runtime.",
    "Protocol: HTTP REST API of the CorePlay at the URL from the config field 'host' (default 'http://192.168.2.140', which is an example value from the source and not a recommendation; regex /^https?:\\/\\/[\\w]+/). Only player 1 is addressed (paths /players/1/...).",
    "Written in TypeScript with shared option objects: OPTIONPLAYBACK (program/preview, default 'program', src/constants.ts:10) is the first option of most entries; transitionType/mode/startPoint lists come from src/constants.ts:44-58; 'Toggle Value' is {id:'toggle'} (constants.ts:35). Entity provenance points at the action/feedback key, not at the shared constants.",
    "Options carry isVisible functions (recorded in visibleWhen as source text). The take actions use only the options named in the 'properties' multidropdown.",
    "Take Duration range 0-600 has no step; the volume step is 3 (dB, as written) while the callback clamps -200..12 and sends two decimals.",
    "The tally feedback 'cue' regex /^\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$|any/ and the setMedia cue regex /^\\d+(\\.\\d+)?|first$/ are as in the source; each has an alternation without grouping, so the anchors only apply to one branch.",
    "setMedia: 'Single Media' (collections) accepts collection 1-255 and slot 1-255 (clamped); 'Playlist' accepts any number >= 1 and a cue like 3 or 3.1 (a whole number is sent as '3.0'); 'first' selects the first cue by CorePlay sort order.",
    "Source quirks kept: the 'Audio: Mute' default 'next' is not a choice.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.11.2: options do not support expressions. Presets (src/presets.ts) and variables are not catalogued."
  ]
}
